{"findings":[{"finding":"The overdue threshold can be configured (REQ-1, AC-1.4 sets it to 10), but the bucket bounds are fixed at 7–30/31–60/61–90/91+, so with a threshold of 3 an invoice 3–6 days overdue is on the list but in no bucket, and with 10 the 7–30 bucket's lower bound is wrong.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The bucket boundaries (7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90, 91) are fixed in the requirement, while the threshold they depend on is a configuration setting (ASM-3/ASM-10), and the two assumptions disagreed on the buckets (ASM-5 vs ASM-14).","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-1 and NFR-2 describe the same performance target at two different data sizes (10,000 invoices/1,000 customers vs 5,000 open invoices/500 customers), with unexplained 'd1' and 'd2/d3' labels, so it is unclear which size is the acceptance target.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-2 and AC-2.1 treat the statuses 'open', paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft and written off as if they exist in the client's invoice data, but the current-behaviour artifact has no claims and no repository was found, so these values have no anchor.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-4 assumes the existing records have a customer name, an amount and a date-only due date, with no anchor; currency, and whether the due date is stored as a timestamp that needs converting to the business timezone, are not addressed.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Only a valid customer with no overdue invoices is covered (AC-5.2); there is no defined response for a customer filter that doesn't exist or is malformed (404 vs 400 vs empty 200).","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only unauthenticated or invalid tokens are covered (401); there is no rule for a request that is authenticated under the existing scheme but is not a staff user (e.g. 403), even though access is limited to 'any authenticated staff user'.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"There is no behaviour for an invalid or missing configured threshold (zero, negative, non-numeric) or business timezone, and no AC for an empty overdue list when no filter is applied.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Existing records that break the assumed shape are not handled: an open invoice whose customer is missing or deleted (no customer name for REQ-4), or a partly paid invoice that is still 'open'.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-3.1 is checked by comparing raw Postgres rows byte for byte against a snapshot, which is a check on database internals rather than anything visible at the API surface.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The ACs refer to 'the overdue list endpoint' and to bucket values without fixing the path (the assumptions give two different placeholder paths), the query parameter names or the format of the bucket values (e.g. how '90+' is sent), so a test can't be written against a concrete API contract.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The spec's assumptions narrow the human's Q-3 answer 'Every attempt, each with a delivery status' to 'every attempt that reaches the provider', so blocked sends (missing email, duplicate, not overdue) are excluded from history, which contradicts the accepted answer.","reqId":"REQ-11","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"This run is limited to REQ-1–REQ-7, but its assumptions fix behaviour for later runs (8 s provider timeout, 60 s double-submit window counted from the previous accepted request, history exclusions, a dropped REQ-20) and say those deferred requirements 'keep their IDs and wording', without that wording being reviewable here.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 60 s double-submit window and the 8 s provider timeout / 10 s endpoint budget are stated as fixed values rather than configuration, even though ASM-13 offered 60 s only as an example ('e.g. 60s').","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":8,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}